Package: bpnmf
Title: Bayesian Panel NMF for Causal Effects on Panel Count Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Alexander", "Franks", email = "afranks@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates causal treatment effects on panel count data (e.g.
    births, low-birth-weight or preterm outcomes by state and period) via a
    Bayesian hierarchical model with a low-rank nonnegative factorization of
    the log-rate surface, fit with Stan through 'cmdstanr'. Supports joint and
    two-stage cut (modular) inference, censored small-count likelihoods,
    posterior predictive checks, and publication tables and figures. An R port
    of the Python package 'bayesian_panel_nmf'.
